According to a new report from Intel Market Research, the North America luxury cosmetics market was valued at USD 18.37 billion in 2024 and is projected to reach USD 23.18 billion by 2034, growing at a CAGR of 3.5% during the forecast period (2026–2034). This growth is driven by increasing disposable incomes, premiumization trends in beauty purchases, and influencer-led digital marketing strategies reshaping consumer behavior.
What are Luxury Cosmetics?
Luxury cosmetics represent the pinnacle of beauty products characterized by high-performance formulations, exquisite packaging, and brand prestige. These premium offerings span makeup (including foundations and lipsticks), advanced skincare (such as anti-aging serums), and prestige fragrances. Unlike mass-market alternatives, luxury cosmetics emphasize clinical-grade ingredients, exclusive distribution channels, and personalized customer experiences that justify their premium pricing.
